# UI-specific Rules

## Slint Design Patterns

For details, refer to `docs/ja/develop/design/ui/slint-patterns.md`.

## Layer Boundaries

For details, refer to `docs/ja/develop/design/ui/layers.md`.

- `.slint` files: layout and display only. No business logic, no domain types.
- `src/adapters/`: pure domain-type <-> Slint-type conversion. No I/O.
- `src/viewmodels/`: UI state, callback implementations, facade calls.

Only ViewModels call `flequit-core` facades. Never call repositories or concrete
infrastructure crates from the UI. Never write `#[cfg(target_os = ...)]` here.

## Responsive Layout

For details, refer to `docs/ja/develop/design/ui/responsive-layout.md`.

Branch on window width (`Compact < 600px`, `Medium 600-1023px`, `Expanded >= 1024px`),
never on target OS. Minimum tap target is 48px in `Compact`.

## Thread Boundary

Slint components and models are not `Send`. Update the UI from background threads
only via `slint::Weak::upgrade_in_event_loop()`. Capture only `Weak` in closures.

## Model Updates

Use row-level notifications (`set_row_data` / `push` / `remove`).
Use `set_vec` only for initial load and filter changes.

## Internationalization System

For details, refer to `docs/ja/develop/design/ui/i18n-system.md`.

All display strings use `@tr()` in `.slint`. Never build user-facing strings in Rust;
pass an identifier and map it to `@tr()` in `ui/globals/i18n.slint`.
